# A `+` whose operand is a STAGED call is refused where it meets a
# kind at a key INSIDE a map; the same sum at the top level stands up,
# and so does one whose operands are both literals. Run:
#   aontu staged-op-under-a-key.aon
# The string spelling below fails the same way and long predates list
# concatenation (ADR-037), which only made the shape worth writing:
#   x: { k: "a", of: string }
#   x: { k: "a", of: "p" + join(["q"], "") }   # not-scalar-type
# It is why `{k:"frag", of:["head"] + emit(...)}` cannot be written
# under aontu:code's schema.
# expected: {"x":{"k":"a","of":["p","q"]}}
# actual:   [aontu/list] at $.x.of
x: { k: "a", of: [&: string] }
x: { k: "a", of: ["p"] + each(["q"], _) }
